<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:58Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>At odds over the EU budget, European leaders cut summit short - DW has more</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e7e09ec8a91b6b035af2e554af3dbaac5a2b634ffecf7e69cb16e49b4adf172e</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T21:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/at-odds-over-the-eu-budget-european-leaders-cut-summit-short-dw-has-more/live-80056415--8778ca45de01.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/at-odds-over-the-eu-budget-european-leaders-cut-summit-short-dw-has-more/live-80056415?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Even before they met, it was clear the gap between European leaders' demands for the EU budget would make negotiations difficult. They ended a summit meeting early and aim to agree on EU funding in December. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Albania's youth are protesting in Flamingo Revolution, not leaving the country anymore</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16e5aa9d3dee4c10d58844d5fe435d988fc9431e379115ff47c90de15ad2fc35</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T20:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/albania-s-youth-are-protesting-in-flamingo-revolution-not-leaving-the-country-anymore/a-80068939--c6558d2b9306.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/albania-s-youth-are-protesting-in-flamingo-revolution-not-leaving-the-country-anymore/a-80068939?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Youth protests against a rigid political system and corruption have shaken the government of Albanian Prime Minister Edi Rama. They also show that fewer young people are willing to emigrate in search of a better future.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Gerard Depardieu to stand trial in France for rape and sexual assault</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34ec917352d81c3fdbd83eef3683c40a41a1e849476c75acb0b1b7d457a975ee</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T20:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gerard-depardieu-to-stand-trial-in-france-for-rape-and-sexual-assault/a-80069424--de01e99588bd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gerard-depardieu-to-stand-trial-in-france-for-rape-and-sexual-assault/a-80069424?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Paris Court of Appeal upheld the order for the 77-year-old French actor to stand trial on charges of raping and sexually assaulting an actress in 2018.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Guinea-Bissau junta delays presidential vote for 2 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a2fec2e30bdf060e15bbbd54f33a5bc333c248a66f83629e9a7e66b441feb57</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T20:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/guinea-bissau-junta-delays-presidential-vote-for-2-years/a-80068910--e34f489a3b6d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/guinea-bissau-junta-delays-presidential-vote-for-2-years/a-80068910?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The decision came exactly one year after the military took power on November 26, 2025. The junta said the conditions were insufficient to hold presidential elections for now.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trial of Berlin woman accused of spying for Russia begins after delay</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8eb055fccdfa9e885d213f14c0694abc98848dba68eb08284309f9232a9c6125</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T17:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trial-of-berlin-woman-accused-of-spying-for-russia-begins-after-delay/a-80057677--743246431230.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trial-of-berlin-woman-accused-of-spying-for-russia-begins-after-delay/a-80057677?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite delays due to health issues, the trial of the Berlin woman accused of spying for Russia has begun. Prosecutors say the defendant used her military contacts to provide information on German defense and Ukraine.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi pop music is thriving — but for the right reasons?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:99ecb0dd0e9b8df356acba04cee5a7b4ed7877f86a2b7d4a739f7b2840aa2f31</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T17:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saudi-pop-music-is-thriving-but-for-the-right-reasons/a-80036013--30f0e598eb37.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saudi-pop-music-is-thriving-but-for-the-right-reasons/a-80036013?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As part of Vision 2030, Saudi Arabia's music scene has evolved hugely thanks to state funding and support. Local musicians and DJs are optimistic. But are they actually just helping prop up an authoritarian state?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>On farewell trip, Steinmeier calls for more investment in Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1960b3548f79614dd634c5fcabc512a2d69ead8890e0fcce3c676a96efb14fbe</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T17:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/on-farewell-trip-steinmeier-calls-for-more-investment-in-africa/a-80067717--a2b49bd3f417.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/on-farewell-trip-steinmeier-calls-for-more-investment-in-africa/a-80067717?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Cote d'Ivoire, Ghana, Kenya: On his last trip to Africa, outgoing German President Frank-Walter Steinmeier called on companies at home to be bolder and seize opportunities in Africa.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says he urged Putin to 'pull back' military aggression in Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:744fc2ac44a3798bda5a839db1490b479cec82d757aacb4f757a3d4ffb386b6b</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T16:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-says-he-urged-putin-to-pull-back-military-aggression-in-europe/a-80067722--6941c482f606.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-says-he-urged-putin-to-pull-back-military-aggression-in-europe/a-80067722?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump claimed that he talked with Vladimir Putin about ceasing Russia's military aggression in Europe and expressed his belief in the possibility of a deal between Russia and Ukraine.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Protests in Iraqi Kurdistan at plans for government in Baghdad to take over oil, border crossings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d52ae0ebca4237aee02f97a34007d334058a475f838981bf47327f8fc21bf561</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T16:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/protests-in-iraqi-kurdistan-at-plans-for-government-in-baghdad-to-take-over-oil-border-crossings/a-80065994--71d95a7c949d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/protests-in-iraqi-kurdistan-at-plans-for-government-in-baghdad-to-take-over-oil-border-crossings/a-80065994?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Thousands have gathered in the capital of northern Iraq's semiautonomous Kurdish region, waving flags and voicing opposition to plans for the federal government to take control of oil operations and border crossings.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: IG Metall union says deal reached with employers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4f7ca7d7dc34ca25b98d44d7da91a7dc4f217f176fda53d82dca22a554f0034</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T15:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-ig-metall-union-says-deal-reached-with-employers/a-80066792--f4aca602c9d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-ig-metall-union-says-deal-reached-with-employers/a-80066792?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">IG Metall, representing millions of workers in Germany's metal and electrical industry, is the country's largest trade union. The deal came after more than 24 hours of talks with employers.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Is authoritarian Vietnam ready to phase out the death penalty?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d16f47922bfe01b25969a0d65b1c42b76fba39f68cbe3cf896a749e2279344d</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T15:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-authoritarian-vietnam-ready-to-phase-out-the-death-penalty/a-80064271--09c5b90052b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-authoritarian-vietnam-ready-to-phase-out-the-death-penalty/a-80064271?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Vietnam has voted to abolish the death penalty for six more crimes, continuing a decades-long trend of restricting capital punishment.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iranian drone kills 2 Italian workers in Kuwait, Meloni says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1656bad786426aac74144097c31b2af60d230fba7945fd3cb61459923dc31377</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T15:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iranian-drone-kills-2-italian-workers-in-kuwait-meloni-says/a-80064974--37bfcbc87429.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iranian-drone-kills-2-italian-workers-in-kuwait-meloni-says/a-80064974?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Italians were employed as technicians for the Italian branch of German arms manufacturer Rheinmetall. One Kuwaiti and one Pakistani national were also injured in the attack. Iran has denied involvement.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's opposition voices face growing pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19a91ce99a138b184d9908282199f45f1dbb684cbd35fbb5745708a5193353e0</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-opposition-voices-face-growing-pressure/a-80063893--fc3fb0c33bdb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-opposition-voices-face-growing-pressure/a-80063893?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Opposition politicians and government critics say arrests, prosecutions and restrictions on public activity are making it harder to challenge those in power. Is a broader pattern emerging?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Freigang banned — Germany star to miss 2027 World Cup</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d66a9d436a5c1bf8f856baae8f2d64ff7aaaf4fc46c82ea21100c3a9442a4fbc</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T14:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/freigang-banned-germany-star-to-miss-2027-world-cup/a-80063930--642807df4daf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/freigang-banned-germany-star-to-miss-2027-world-cup/a-80063930?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany forward Laura Freigang has been suspended until October 2027 after missing three doping tests, ruling her out of next year's Women's World Cup in Brazil. Freigang has denied any intention to evade controls.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>FIFA says a cyberattack against it targeted a 'limited set of personal and business information'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c72c639b16dfb5adca6923f52812511bcaa34ee7d054caeb6865b8ee604f3483</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T14:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fifa-says-a-cyberattack-against-it-targeted-a-limited-set-of-personal-and-business-information/a-80062660--002158da7f55.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fifa-says-a-cyberattack-against-it-targeted-a-limited-set-of-personal-and-business-information/a-80062660?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">World football's governing body says the cyberattack targeted personal and business information. They struck at a sensitive time for the under-fire organization and its president, Gianni Infantino.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU-Indonesia trade deal opens new markets, but challenges remain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08a7589f82f8036ce41acb98c01ed69e90146a82074579ce9d49b177991191ff</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T13:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-indonesia-trade-deal-opens-new-markets-but-challenges-remain/a-80059568--6d93bfcf9a92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-indonesia-trade-deal-opens-new-markets-but-challenges-remain/a-80059568?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The agreement offers new export and investment opportunities for Jakarta and Brussels. But can Indonesia turn Europe's growing interest in its markets and critical minerals into sustainable gains at home?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Joshua Kimmich critcizes Bayern bosses over Musiala health comments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce64c23f826b720a320c10f1bbd9a2e8115d26ff4af063bd7434e08fe2456ee0</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T12:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/joshua-kimmich-critcizes-bayern-bosses-over-musiala-health-comments/a-80060155--f8755c2422c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/joshua-kimmich-critcizes-bayern-bosses-over-musiala-health-comments/a-80060155?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Joshua Kimmich has slammed Bayern Munich's leadership over comments about Jamal Musiala's health issues. The bosses have questioned whether the player can return to previous form – and is still worth his high salary.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Crew member dies after diesel tanker sinks off Ibiza coast</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13923b7023ac949f9ff5296fb08e8a9878c9ab4df295ae652b093823502a231e</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T11:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/crew-member-dies-after-diesel-tanker-sinks-off-ibiza-coast/a-80059054--ee7eaa5aee4e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/crew-member-dies-after-diesel-tanker-sinks-off-ibiza-coast/a-80059054?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities rescued 17 crew members but one later died in hospital after a diesel tanker capsized off the Spanish island of Ibiza. A contingency plan against possible pollution damage is now in place.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What is the US permitting bill and would it actually help the climate?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:90dde568aebc37b51144934890a46338401db0c9a7e3ed93dde35f3d3dee2611</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T11:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-is-the-us-permitting-bill-and-would-it-actually-help-the-climate/a-80007213--5f9c9611007b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-is-the-us-permitting-bill-and-would-it-actually-help-the-climate/a-80007213?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sweeping US legislation to speed up energy projects has found rare bipartisan support. Supporters say it would unlock clean energy and lower energy bills, but critics say it's a gift to fossil fuels.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Cologne court awards record damages in Catholic sex abuse case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1bf71b34baf6b9f90d43c7497d2d7d5fddfba733b38448d67aa3627c8a6d8c29</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T09:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-cologne-court-awards-record-damages-in-catholic-sex-abuse-case/live-80056746--18122980124b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-cologne-court-awards-record-damages-in-catholic-sex-abuse-case/live-80056746?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A court has awarded the highest damages ever in Germany to a victim of sexual abuse linked with the Catholic Church. An alleged spy and suspected terrorists are also making headlines in Germany on Thursday. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: 2 arrested, suspected of plotting synagogue attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2031682ec8e92e713a30596e1b546a9e22789f2a5dcd8aba629599eba2ac5877</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T09:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-2-arrested-suspected-of-plotting-synagogue-attack/a-80057715--3c7a6577a7d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-2-arrested-suspected-of-plotting-synagogue-attack/a-80057715?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Federal prosecutors say they have ordered the arrest of two members of a pro-Iranian group on suspicion of planning an attack on a synagogue. They were detained in the cities of Heidelberg and Cologne.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
